  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n2026 Lake Delhi Trustee Election (July 21, 2026) - Elections - Delaware County, Iowa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n Delaware County\n Iowa • Elections\n \n \n\n \n\n Facebook Contact Us\n \n \n\n \n \nHome\n \nVote \n \n \nRegister to Vote\n \nAbsentee Voting\n \nMaps\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nPrecincts\n \nVoter ID\n \n \n \nElections \n \n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n \n \n \nElected Officials \n \n \nFederal\n \nState\n \nCounty\n \nCity\n \nSchool Board\n \nTownship\n \n \n \nCandidates\n \nNews\n \nFAQ\n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n Delaware County\nElections\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nElections 2026 Lake Delhi Trustee Election\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nElections by Year\n\n \n2026 \n2025 \n2024 \n2023 \n2022 \n2021 \n2020 \n2019 \n2018 \n2017 \n2016 \n2015 \n2014 \n2013 \n2012 \n2011 \n2010 \n2009 \n2008 \nView All\n\n\nElections\n\n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n\n \n \n\n \n2026 Lake Delhi Trustee Election\n\n \nJuly 21, 2026\n Special Election \n \n\n A Special Election is any election that is not regularly scheduled. A special election may be held for any purpose authorized or required by law; often to fill a vacancy or for a public measure. \n\n \n \n \n \n\n \nElection Results\n \n\n Download Official Results \n \n \n\n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \nArchived Election Details\n \nLAKE DELHI COMBINED RECEREATION FACILITY AND WATER QUALITY DISTRICT ELECTION  \n \n\n                                District Trustee (three (3) positions)                                        3 year terms \n \n\n  \n \n\n  \n \n\nPolling Location: \n \n\nSt. John's Parish \n \n\n303 South St \n \n\nDelhi, IA 52223 \n \n\n  \n \n\nPoll Hours: \n \n\n12:00 p.m. (noon) to 8:00 p.m. \n \n\n  \n \n\nPre-Election Day Voter Registration \n \n\nPre-Election Day voter registration for this election will close Monday, July 6, 2026 at 5:00 p.m.  It is highly recommended that those persons wishing to vote in this election should pre-register on or before the July 6th deadline.   \n \n\nElection Day Voter Registration \n \n\nEligible persons have the right to register to vote and cast a ballot on Election Day if they are able to provide proof of both their identity and residency at the polls.  Please bring a valid and current photo ID which has an expiration date.  If the address on your ID is not your current lake address, you will need to prove residency.  The following documents can be used as proof of residency if they contain your name and current lake address, and are current within 45 days:  Residential lease, utility bill, bank statement, paycheck, government check or other government document, or a property tax statement (current within 45 days of payment date). \n \n\nProof of ID \n \n\nIf you do not have an Iowa driver’s license, you may use a photo ID that is current, valid, and contains an expiration date. The following are acceptable IDs: \n \n \n \nIowa non-operator ID \n \nOut-of-state driver’s license or non-operator ID \n \nU.S. passport \n \nU.S. military or veteran ID \n \nID card issued by employer \n \nStudent ID issued by Iowa high school or college \n \nTribal ID card/document \n \n \n\nProof of Residence \n \n\nIf the address on your photo ID is not your current lake address, you may use another document (paper or electronic format) to prove where you live if it contains your name and current address and is current within 45 days. The following are acceptable proofs of residence: \n \n \n \nResidential lease \n \nUtility bill (including a cell phone bill) \n \nBank statement \n \nPaycheck \n \nGovernment check or other government document \n \nProperty tax statement (current within 45 days of final payment date) \n \n \n\nAbsentee Voting \n \n \n \nAbsentee voting by mail, to request an absentee ballot for this election, use this absentee ballot request form Absentee Ballot Request Form    The absentee ballot request form is also available at the Delaware County Auditor's Office,  or at the Iowa Secretary of State’s website at  https://sos.iowa.gov/.  You must complete this form and mail it to the Delaware County Commissioner of Elections, 301 E. Main St., Room 210, Manchester, Iowa 52057.  The first day to request an absentee ballot is Tuesday, May 12, 2026. The first day ballots can be mailed to voters is Wednesday, July 1, 2026. The last day to request an absentee ballot by mail is Monday, July 7, 2025 at 5:00 p.m. \n \nAbsentee voting In-person will be available at the Delaware County Auditor’s Office begining Wednesday, July 1, 2026 at 8:00 a.m. through Tuesday, July 21, 2026 at 11:00 a.m.  If you have any questions regarding this process, please contact the Delaware County Auditor’s Office at 563-927-4701. \n \nCurbside Absentee voting is available at the Delaware County Courthouse begining Wednesday, July 1, 2026 at 8:00 a.m. through  Tuesday, July 21, 2026 at 11:00 a.m. as well. Please contact the Delaware County Auditor's Office at 563-927-4701 if you would like to vote with this service.  \n \n \n\nPoll Hours at St. John's Parish  \n \n \n \nTuesday July 21, 2026 from 12:00 p.m. (noon) to 8:00 p.m.  \n \n \n\nCurbside voting is also available at St. John's Parish - 303 South St. on Election Day.  If you have any questions regarding the process, please contact the Delaware County Auditor’s Office by phone at 563-927-4701 or by e-mail at auditor@co.delaware.ia.us.  \n \n\nThe polling place designated for use in this election is accessible to persons with disabilities.  However, any voter who is physically unable to enter a polling place has the right to vote in the voter’s vehicle.  \n \n \n\n \nSample Ballots (PDF)\n \n\n Sample Ballot\n \n \n\n \nBack: Past Elections\n \n \n\n\n\n\nThis webpage was printed on October 17, 2026. For the most current election-related information, visit the Delaware County, Iowa, Elections website at https://delawarecountyelections.iowa.gov.\n\n\n \n\n Delaware County Courthouse\n\n 301 E Main St, Manchester, IA 52057\n\n Contact Us\n\n Accessibility\n\n Delaware County Website\n \n \nOffice Hours\n\n Monday - Friday \n \n8:00 AM - 4:30 PM \n \nContact Numbers\n\n Phone: (563) 927-4701\n \nFax: (563) 927-6423 \n \n\n \n\n Facebook Contact Us\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \npowered by \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"
